// Jobs that ended Failed, per handler.
// Backs the "jobs are dead-lettering" alert: a job ends Failed when its handler reports a failure
// that retrying cannot mend or when its last attempt failed, and its requester (else the tenant's
// administrators) is notified. A handful is normal; a rising share on one handler is a defect or an
// outage of what it depends on. Above 5% of a handler's completions, or more than 20, is a starting
// point.
customMetrics
| where name == "tellma.jobs.completed"
| extend outcome = tostring(customDimensions["outcome"])
| extend handler = tostring(customDimensions["handler"])
| summarize
    failed = sumif(valueSum, outcome == "failed"),
    total = sum(valueSum)
    by handler, bin(timestamp, 15m)
| where failed > 20 or (failed > 0 and failed * 20 > total)
